          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bāoguǒ is built from bāo and guǒ, both inherited from Middle Chinese, paew and kwaX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription); the dictionary glosses the second 'to wrap, to bind', and gives the pair itself as the gloss of the first."
            }
          ]
        },
